      "type": "msg",
      "id": "5a161bec-9667-46ac-b59d-8715a8cacec7",
      "body": "I want to use the Surya architecture to test it's abilities against the baseline of hemispheric chirality of filaments. I understand that the baseline already scores really well since hemispheres are highly associated with certain chiralities. I have a catalog of 45 filament events and they are labeled with hemisphere (north or south) and I also know the chirality of them (dextral or sinestral). I would like to come up with a baseline to use in the surya_workshop/downstream_apps/filament_kyle/1_baseline_template.ipynb notebook.",
      "sender": "kwebster",
      "metadata": {
        "settings": {},
        "to_persona": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
        "model": {
          "settings": {},
          "id": "sonnet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "mentions": [],
      "type": "msg",
      "time": 1789500115.2814105,
      "body": "I'll look at the existing structure to understand the baseline pattern used elsewhere in the repo before building yours.",
      "id": "a35e5e0b-2bfb-4043-88dd-897a300e6bdf",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false
    },
