      "body": "I now have the full picture. Quick recap of where things stand and what's still open before I build this:\n\n**Current state**\n- `configs.py` and `datasets/filament_dataset.py` are already wired for a hemisphere label (0/1), matched by timestamp to the Surya index \u2014 that plumbing works.\n- `data/fil_data.csv` has only 11 debug rows with `start_time, hemisphere` \u2014 no chirality column yet, and it's not your real 45-event catalog.\n- `1_baseline_template.ipynb` is still an unmodified copy of the flare-regression template (imports `FlareDSDataset`, `RegressionFlareModel`, trains a linear regression via Lightning to predict flare flux) \u2014 none of it has been adapted for this task yet.\n- Your earlier brainstorming already reached the key scientific call: since Martin's Rule predicts chirality from hemisphere alone at ~90% accuracy, the right baseline is that fixed rule itself (zero trainable parameters, can't overfit) \u2014 not a trained model, which would be meaningless noise at N=45.\n\n**Two things I need from you before I build this:**\n\n1. **Real catalog data.** I don't have your 45 filament events with chirality labels anywhere in this repo \u2014 only the 11-row hemisphere-only stub. Can you paste/provide the `(start_time, hemisphere, chirality)` rows so I can populate `data/fil_data.csv` for real? (Or if you'd rather add them yourself, I can build everything else against the stub schema and you drop in the real rows after.)\n\n2. **Baseline design confirmation.** Given the N=45/Martin's Rule reasoning above, I'm planning to make `1_baseline_template.ipynb` compute the trivial hemisphere\u2192chirality rule directly on the catalog \u2014 no image loading, no Lightning training loop \u2014 rather than following the flare-template's \"train a linear model\" pattern. This is a deliberate departure from that template. Does that match what you want, or did you want the baseline to still go through the Surya dataset/dataloader machinery (