    {
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "All three edits are in place:\n\n1. **`datasets/filament_dataset.py`** \u2014 label source switched from `hemisphere` to `chirality` (0 = dextral, 1 = sinistral), with the dead commented-out mapping code removed.\n2. **`datasets/filament_dataset.py`** \u2014 `__getitem__` now also returns `sample[\"hemisphere\"]` as passthrough metadata (the `\"forecast\"` key is untouched, still holds the label).\n3. **`configs/config_script.yaml`** \u2014 `filament_index_path` now points to `../data/basic_fil_data.csv`.\n\nDocstrings were also updated to describe chirality/hemisphere instead of the stale flare-intensity language they inherited from the template.\n\nReady to move on to `1_baseline_template.ipynb`: do you want the baseline to be a trivial Martin's-Rule lookup (predict chirality directly from `hemisphere`, no image loading or training), or should it follow the template's full Lightning-trained pattern like the flare-forecast baseline does?",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
