      "time": 1789565895.7324274,
      "body": "Yes \u2014 confirmed directly from the CSV, not inferred. `surya_aws_s3_val.csv` breaks into contiguous blocks when I look at the gaps between consecutive timestamps, and every single block is the same 15-day window, just in a different year:\n\n```\n2011-01-16 -> 2011-01-30\n2013-01-16 -> 2013-01-30\n2014-01-16 -> 2014-01-30\n2015-01-16 -> 2015-01-30\n2016-01-16 -> 2016-01-30\n2017-01-16 -> 2017-01-30\n2018-01-16 -> 2018-01-30\n2019-01-16 -> 2019-01-30\n2020-01-16 -> 2020-01-30\n2021-01-16 -> 2021-01-30\n2023-01-16 -> 2023-01-30\n2024-01-16 -> 2024-01-30\n```\n\nSo yes \u2014 the val split is Jan 16\u201330 of each year and nothing else. It's not a bug, it's a deliberate held-out slice for generic Surya validation, it just happens to be a slice your filament catalog (March/April/June/July/Sept/Nov events) never touches.\n\nWorth noting: 2012 is also completely absent from that list \u2014 val skips straight from 2011 to 2013. Same gap I found in the train index. So this isn't only a val problem.",
