      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "body": "From the year-by-year breakdown of `surya_aws_s3_train.csv`:\n\n```\n2010    27959   (partial year \u2014 starts 2010-05-13)\n2011    36600\n2012         \u2014  missing\n2013    36600\n2014    36600\n2015    36600\n2016    36720\n2017    36600\n2018    36600\n2019    36600\n2020    36720\n2021    36600\n2022         \u2014  missing\n2023    36600\n2024    36601\n```\n\nSo train covers 2010 (partial) through 2024, at the full ~12-minute cadence (~36,600/year), **except two full years are absent: 2012 and 2022.**\n\nThat directly explains the earlier mismatch: 9 of your 11 catalog events are dated in 2012, so none of them have any Surya timestep to align to in train \u2014 not just val. Only the 2013-11-07 and 2015-03-15 events have a shot at matching (and when I merge-asof'd against train earlier, those two did match, within a few minutes each).\n\nSo right now, train \u222a val together can support at most 2 of your 11 labeled events \u2014 the rest have no corresponding Surya frame at all under these indices, regardless of tolerance or which split you use.",
