    {
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "time": 1789567008.4308121,
      "mentions": [],
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "`train samples: 3` is wrong \u2014 it should be 11 (all of them, since I built the index to match exactly). Here's why only 3 survived, and it's a bug in the index file I built, not in `build_helio_dataloaders`.\n\n**The direction mismatch:** `ds_match_direction: forward` means (per the comment in the config, and confirmed in `filament_dataset.py`'s `merge_asof(..., direction=ds_match_direction)`): for each *Surya frame*, find the next *catalog event at or after it* \u2014 i.e. Surya timestep \u2264 event time. That's \"use the solar state *before* the flare/event\" \u2014 causal.\n\n**What I actually built:** for each event, I looked up the nearest S3 file **after** the event's timestamp (I was thinking \"closest available frame to the event,\" not \"which side of the event does this pipeline require\"). So every Surya timestep in my index is a few minutes *after* its corresponding event, not before.\n\n**The effect:** `merge_asof` for each Surya timestep looks forward for the *next* catalog event \u2265 that timestep \u2014 but since my timestep is already past its \"own\" event, it skips that event and latches onto whatever the *next* event chronologically happens to be, if one exists within 2 days. That's exactly the mismatch you can see in the printed batch: `ds_index: ['2012-03-07T01:30:06', '2012-03-07T00:24:06']` \u2014 those two March 7 events (12 hours apart) got cross-matched to *each other's* Surya frames. All other events had no \"next event\" within 2 days, so they were dropped, leaving only 3 spurious survivors.\n\n**The fix:** rebuild the index using the nearest S3 frame **at or before** each event's timestamp (backward-nearest), not after. Want me to redo the lookup that way and re-run this same test before touching the file?",
      "id": "461b1b29-5981-4944-ac4a-37f5a5892ac4",
      "type": "msg"
    },
    {
      "id": "89bb4e4f-f703-4971-b063-bbd8b0637739",
      "metadata": {
        "to_persona": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
        "model": {
          "id": null,
          "settings": {}
        },
        "settings": {}
      },
      "sender": "kwebster",
      "type": "msg",
      "raw_time": false,
      "time": 1789568082.3008761,
      "body": "Yeah, remake the csv file with the timestamps that match correctly with the match directions that work for all 11 events"
    },
    {
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "",
      "metadata": {
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "raw_input": {
              "command": "source /srv/conda/etc/profile.d/conda.sh && conda activate /home/jovyan/envs/surya_ws && cd /home/jovyan/surya_workshop && python3 << 'EOF'\nimport boto3, pandas as pd\nfrom botocore import UNSIGNED\nfrom botocore.config import Config\n\ns3 = boto3.client('s3', config=Config(signature_version=UNSIGNED))\n\nevents = [\n    \"2012-03-05T04:00:05\",\n    \"2012-03-07T00:24:06\",\n    \"2012-03-07T01:30:06\",\n    \"2012-03-13T17:36:05\",\n    \"2012-03-15T07:12:05\",\n    \"2012-04-23T18:24:05\",\n    \"2012-06-14T14:12:07\",\n    \"2012-07-12T16:48:05\",\n    \"2012-09-28T00:12:05\",\n    \"2013-11-07T15:12:10\",\n    \"2015-03-15T01:48:05\",\n]\n\ndef list_day(dt):\n    prefix = f\"{dt.year:04d}/{dt.month:02d}/{dt.year:04d}{dt.month:02d}{dt.day:02d}_\"\n    paginator = s3.get_paginator('list_objects_v2')\n    keys = []\n    for page in paginator.paginate(Bucket='nasa-surya-bench', Prefix=prefix):\n        for obj in page.get('Contents', []):\n            keys.append(obj['Key'])\n    return sorted(keys)\n\ndef parse_times(keys):\n    out = []\n    for k in keys:\n        fname = k.split('/')[-1]\n        datepart, timepart = fname.replace('.nc', '').split('_')\n        t = pd.Timestamp(f\"{datepart[:4]}-{datepart[4:6]}-{datepart[6:8]} {timepart[:2]}:{timepart[2:4]}:00\")\n        out.append((t, k))\n    return out\n\nrows = []\nfor e in events:\n    ts = pd.Timestamp(e)\n    times_keys = parse_times(list_day(ts))\n    back = sorted([tk for tk in times_keys if tk[0] <= ts])\n    if not back:\n        ts_prev = ts - pd.Timedelta(days=1)\n        times_keys += parse_times(list_day(ts_prev))\n        back = sorted([tk for tk in times_keys if tk[0] <= ts])\n    match_t, match_k = back[-1]  # latest one <= event time\n    delta = ts - match_t\n    rows.append({\n        \"event_start_time\": e,\n        \"path\": f\"s3://nasa-surya-bench/{match_k}\",\n        \"timestep\": match_t,\n        \"present\": 1,\n        \"dayofyear\": match_t.dayofyear,\n        \"delta_before_event\": str(delta),\n    })\n\ndf = pd.DataFrame(rows)\nprint(df[[\"event_start_time\",\"timestep\",\"delta_before_event\"]].to_string())\n\nout_df = df[[\"path\",\"timestep\",\"present\",\"dayofyear\"]].sort_values(\"timestep\").reset_index(drop=True)\nout_path = \"downstream_apps/filament_kyle/data/surya_index_filament_events.csv\"\nout_df.to_csv(out_path, index=False)\nprint(\"\\nWrote\", out_path)\nEOF\n"
            },
            "permission_options": [
              {
                "name": "Yes",
                "kind": "allow_once",
                "option_id": "allow-once"
              },
              {
                "name": "No",
                "option_id": "reject",
                "kind": "reject_once"
              }
            ],
