      "id": "24776e99-28af-4ee3-8967-8ef953cdc55c",
      "mentions": [],
      "body": "Commenting out is the wrong fix here \u2014 it leaves dead code sitting in the notebook that will confuse whoever opens it next. The real issue is that the middle section (from the `FilamentDataset`/dataloader build cell through `trainer.fit`) is leftover flare-forecast template: it still points at the original `train_data_path`/`valid_data_path` (missing 2012, hence the error), and it wraps a `RegressionFlareModel`/MSE-loss Lightning setup meant for continuous flare intensity \u2014 not a fit for a binary chirality label. Since neither baseline you just added needs any of that machinery, I'd recommend deleting that whole PyTorch Lightning section rather than disabling it, unless you specifically want to keep a trainable model (e.g., a logistic regression head) around as a third baseline to compare against later \u2014 let me know which and I'll make the cut.",
