      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "All outputs are confirmed correct and saved. `1_baseline_filament.ipynb` is complete: it's a standalone notebook containing only the setup, coin-flip Monte Carlo baseline, and calibrated leave-one-out Martin's Rule baseline \u2014 no Lightning/model/trainer machinery. It's bound to the `conda-env-jovyan-surya_ws-py` kernel (now properly registered with the server) and runs end-to-end with the same results as the appended cells in `1_baseline_template.ipynb`: coin-flip mean accuracy 0.500, calibrated Martin's Rule 0.818 (9/11), on 11 matched catalog events. `1_baseline_template.ipynb` itself was left untouched.\n\nOne thing worth knowing: the Jupyter server was previously missing the `conda-env-jovyan-surya_ws-py` kernelspec (only the base `python3` kernel, without torch, was registered), which is likely why cells in `1_baseline_template.ipynb` were hanging/failing silently. I registered that kernelspec via `ipykernel install` in the `surya_ws` env, so it should now be selectable for any notebook, including the template if you want to try running it again.",
