      "body": "There's no separate Monitor task still running \u2014 `ListAgents` shows no active background tasks in this session. That polling monitor was the one flagged earlier as giving a false-positive \"DONE\" (it matched on a stale `execution_count` from before the kernel switch), so it isn't a reliable source here.\n\nI already re-verified directly by reading the actual cell outputs after the kernel fix, which is authoritative. Final results from `1_baseline_filament.ipynb`:\n\n- **Dataset**: 11 catalog events matched to a Surya frame. Chirality \u2014 dextral (0): 9, sinistral (1): 2. Hemisphere \u2014 south (0): 4, north (1): 7.\n- **Coin-flip baseline** (100,000 Monte Carlo trials): mean accuracy 0.500.\n- **Calibrated Martin's Rule (leave-one-out)**: accuracy 0.818 (9/11).\n\nThe diagnostic kernel-check cell has been removed, so the notebook now contains only the intended baseline content (setup, coin-flip, calibrated Martin's Rule, summary) with no Lightning/model machinery, and runs cleanly end-to-end on the `conda-env-jovyan-surya_ws-py` kernel.",
